# 3: inference reversal, not finding life by combining two badges.
loc1=place('ripple-window','Ripple window','A nearby exposed sandy surface carries ripple shapes. Their shape alone cannot establish that water formed them.')
loc2=place('gravel-window','Gravel window','A nearby intact ledge exposes rounded gravel cemented in rock, with layer geometry visible behind it. No claim of modern liquid water.')
ss=[stock('context-board','Context board','A field board for keeping two source locations distinct.'),stock('two-cell-case','Two-cell comparison case','A ready field case with two separately labelled recesses.'),stock('ripple-cast-sheet','Ripple impression sheet','A mission-approved dry mould sheet for a small non-destructive surface impression; no liquid chemistry.'),stock('loose-gravel-chip','Loose gravel chip','An already detached conglomerate chip at the gravel ledge. It stays associated with that exact source.'),stock('comparison-sleeve','Comparison sleeve','An archival sleeve for the comparison photographs and diagram.')]
